# Copy this file to .env and fill in real values.
# .env is gitignored and must NEVER be committed. This file (.env.example) is committed
# as a template so every team member knows which variables are required.
#
# POLICY: every variable listed here is actually read by the code. Settings that
# were previously documented here but never read (DATABASE_PATH, API_HOST,
# API_PORT) were removed on 2026-10-05 — see "Not configurable via .env" below.
# tests/test_reproducibility.py fails if a variable appears here that no module
# reads, so this list cannot silently drift again.

# --- API Authentication ---
# Required by app/services/auth_service.py. Every request to a protected endpoint
# (all endpoints except GET /health) must include this value in the X-API-Key header.
# Use any non-trivial string for local development; do not reuse it elsewhere.
# Read from the process environment at request time.
API_KEY=replace-with-a-real-key-before-running-locally

# --- Model artifact paths (both optional) ---
# Issue #14 made the artifact paths configurable so they do not depend on one
# developer's machine. If unset, both default to the repo-standard locations, so
# no .env entry is needed to run the project as documented.
#
# MODEL_PATH            — read by predict.py at import time (joblib.load).
#                         Default: models/best_model.pkl
# MODEL_METRICS_PATH    — read by app/services/metrics_service.py at import time.
#                         Default: evaluation/model_comparison.md
#
# app/main.py calls load_dotenv() BEFORE importing the router, so values set here
# are visible to both import-time readers. (Before 2026-10-05 the router was
# imported first, which meant MODEL_METRICS_PATH in .env was silently ignored;
# only a real exported environment variable — e.g. the Dockerfile's ENV — worked.)
MODEL_PATH=models/best_model.pkl
MODEL_METRICS_PATH=evaluation/model_comparison.md

# --- Not configurable via .env (do not add these back without wiring them) ---
# Database path : database/db_connection.py hardcodes Path("database/churn.db"),
#                 relative to the process working directory. Nothing reads
#                 DATABASE_PATH; changing it here would have had no effect.
# API host/port : uvicorn CLI flags own these — `uvicorn app.main:app --host
#                 0.0.0.0 --port 8000`. Nothing reads API_HOST/API_PORT.
#                 (The Makefile's API_PORT is a make variable, not an env var.)
# Streamlit URL : streamlit-app.py reads API_URL (default http://localhost:8000).
#                 That demo path is optional and unverified — it is deliberately
#                 not listed as a required setting above.
